Everything under this directory comes from the UCDP Georeferenced Event
Dataset (GED), published by the Uppsala Conflict Data Program, Department of
Peace and Conflict Research, Uppsala University, at
https://ucdp.uu.se/downloads/ (older releases at
https://ucdp.uu.se/downloads/olddw.html).

UCDP's download page, read on 2026-10-02, says that all its datasets are free
of charge and licensed under CC BY 4.0, and that users are free to use and
redistribute them provided they cite the relevant publications listed with
each dataset. The publications to cite for each release are listed in
README.md beside this file. The codebooks of the releases carry no licence
text of their own.

The files under raw/<version>/ are UCDP's own zip and codebook, byte for
byte; each release's MANIFEST.json records their URLs, sizes, sha256 and
Last-Modified.

The Parquet under parquet/<version>/ was made from the CSV in the zip:

  - columns were typed by name (ids, counts and deaths as integers, latitude
    and longitude as floats, date_start and date_end as timestamps,
    active_year as a boolean); every other column is the text of the CSV
  - a point geometry (WGS 84) was added from longitude and latitude
  - rows were sorted by country_id, date_start and id
  - values were not changed

The source_* columns quote news reports (outlet, date, headline) as UCDP
distributes them. Whether UCDP holds the rights to license those headlines
was not checked.

The code that fetches, checks and converts is MIT, in the repository this
dataset was built from (https://github.com/yuiseki/ucdp-ged), and does not
apply here.
